  ],
  "details": "<p>Great Chesters Roman fort was the\u00a0ninth fort on\u00a0<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hadrian%27s_Wall\" title=\"Hadrian's Wall\">Hadrian's Wall</a>, located between\u00a0<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vercovicium\" title=\"Vercovicium\">Vercovicium</a>\u00a0(Housesteads) to the east and\u00a0<a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnis_(Carvoran)\" title=\"Magnis (Carvoran)\">Magnis (Carvoran)</a>\u00a0to the west. Its likely purpose was to protect the Caw Gap.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "(A)Esica, also known as Great Chesters, was a fort on the line of Hadrian's Wall.",
